course: dictionary
lesson: 11653
title: One word, many meanings: arts
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word arts can mean more than one thing, so use the words around it to work out which meaning fits. «We spent the morning on arts and crafts, making clay pots and paper models.» Here arts means making things by hand.
explain: «She wants to study the arts at university, so she will read history and literature.» Here arts means school subjects about people and culture, not sciences like biology or physics. Ask yourself: is the sentence about making things, or about subjects you study?
explain: «He practises the arts of baking and sewing every weekend.» Here arts is the plural of art and means skills. Try your meaning in the sentence: if "skills" fits, you have the right one.
fact: Arts is a noun, and it can also be the plural of art.
fact: The arts are activities like painting, drawing, music, dance, drama, film and writing, where people make things to express ideas and feelings.
fact: «Arts and crafts» means making things by hand, like collages, paper models and clay pots.
fact: «Martial arts» are fighting sports like karate and judo.
fact: In school, arts can mean subjects about people and culture, like history and languages, as opposed to sciences.
exercise: «We spent the morning on arts and crafts, making paper models.» What does arts and crafts mean here? | Solving maths puzzles | *Making things by hand | Reading about the stars | Running races in the park
exercise: «Her favourite part of the school day is the performing arts, when the class sings and acts on stage.» What are the performing arts? | Sums and spelling tests | Fighting sports like judo | Science experiments in a lab | *Music, dance and drama on a stage
exercise: «He is learning the martial arts, and on Saturdays he trains in karate.» What does martial arts mean? | Painting pictures outdoors | *Fighting sports like karate and judo | Singing in a choir | Making paper models
test: «Mia wants to study the arts at university, so she will read history and literature.» In this sentence, arts means? | Plants and animals | Fighting sports | *Subjects about people and culture, not sciences | Painting and drawing with paints
test: «Dad says the arts of baking bread take years to learn.» What does arts mean in this sentence? | Lessons in a laboratory | Sports played on a field | Subjects about the sea | *Skills
exam: Which of these is NOT one of the arts? | Dance | Painting | Film | *Learning the periodic table
